Go.dot patch 0003 for JUCE: an XML document cannot read other files, nest without end, or expand without end.

JUCE's own fixes, in 8.0.17-security (and 9.0.5), taken verbatim from that tag:
  d383026706fc "XmlDocument: Only load external entities through a
               caller-supplied InputSource" (f8a5c5d80f3b on develop, Tom Poole, 2026-10-20)
  9985d048df0b "XmlDocument: Limit entity expansion and element nesting depth"
               (3342d409111e on develop, Tom Poole, 2026-10-20)
These two files are the same at this pin as at 8.0.16-security, so each is
8.0.17-security's own, with Go.dot's notice after JUCE's licence block.

The faults: a document parsed from a File could name any file on the machine as
its external DTD subset, and the parser read it - so a show file someone sends
could pull a local file's text into the show it becomes. Elements nested deep
enough overflowed the stack, one recursion a level, and entities expanded
without limit (the "billion laughs"). Go.dot parses with XmlDocument show files
(CanonicalXml.cpp, Bundle.cpp, EphemeralState.cpp), Ableton .als sets
(AlsReader.cpp), and its own settings and plugin lists.

What changes for Go.dot: nothing it writes. A document is refused when elements
nest more than 256 deep, entities more than 40, or expansion builds more than
8 MB that is also 100 times the document; external entities are left unexpanded
unless the caller supplies an InputSource, which Go.dot never does. Not taken:
9.0.5's 94410931f43f, "Fix double expansion of escaped references inside entity
markup", which is not in 8.0.17 - a correctness fix for documents declaring
entities, and Go.dot's documents declare none.

LINE ENDINGS. JUCE stores these files with CRLF in its own repository, so every
line of the hunks below ends in CRLF and must stay so; .gitattributes keeps this
file byte for byte (-text), and scripts/patches.py writes it as bytes.

Applied by Go.dot's build, cmake/WfgJucePatches.cmake, in the order
patches/JUCE/series gives; refreshed from the working tree with
scripts/patches.py JUCE refresh, which keeps this header. Against JUCE
37c894f83d37 (8.0.13+7, the JUCE Tracktion Engine 13b5132 pins). Drop it when
the pin moves to 8.0.17, 9.0.5 or later. The author's decision of 2026-11-02.

